# XWLightOS: /etc/environment must exist.
#
# The Seewo manager backend unit com.seewo.terminalmanager.service
# declares EnvironmentFile=/etc/environment WITHOUT the optional '-'
# prefix, so systemd refuses to start the service at all when this
# file is missing (no dash = missing file is a hard error, not a
# silent skip). The live image previously shipped no such file, which
# is a prime suspect for "manager backend autostart never comes up"
# (user report 2026-10-24): Restart=always would only spin a service
# that can never start. An empty file is a valid environment file.
